From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clang.ref.riscv64: silence benign --gcc-toolchain warning

The build failed while compiling cpp/daal/src/services/*.cpp (the
first objects make -j reaches):

    clang++: error: argument unused during compilation:
    '--gcc-toolchain=/usr' [-Werror,-Wunused-command-line-argument]

dev/make/common.mk always derives --gcc-toolchain from `which gcc`
and passes it to every clang compile (C.COMPILE), and
clang.ref.riscv64.mk's COMPILER.lnx.clang turns on -Werror. On this
riscv64 manylinux image, clang's GCCInstallation probe does not
treat that hint as applicable to every translation unit (notably
ones that pull in no libstdc++ headers, like these services/*.cpp
files), so clang reports the otherwise-harmless, driver-level
"unused" notice for them and -Werror turns it into a hard stop. The
same --gcc-toolchain mechanism is exercised unconditionally for
every clang platform (x86_64, arm, ...); only riscv64 hits this,
consistent with clang's RISC-V GCCInstallation detection being a
newer, less-trodden path than the other architectures'.

Add -Wno-unused-command-line-argument next to the existing -Werror
in COMPILER.lnx.clang so this one diagnostic stays non-fatal; it does
not change which headers/libraries get searched or used, only
whether the driver's "unused argument" notice can fail the build.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64/our-infra: clang's GCCInstallation detection quirk on this manylinux image, irrelevant to upstream's x86_64-host cross-compile CI]
---
 dev/make/compiler_definitions/clang.ref.riscv64.mk | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dev/make/compiler_definitions/clang.ref.riscv64.mk b/dev/make/compiler_definitions/clang.ref.riscv64.mk
index 5f81627..a942888 100644
--- a/dev/make/compiler_definitions/clang.ref.riscv64.mk
+++ b/dev/make/compiler_definitions/clang.ref.riscv64.mk
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ COMPILER.sysroot = $(if $(SYSROOT),--sysroot $(SYSROOT))
 
 COMPILER.lnx.clang= clang++ \
                      -DDAAL_REF -DONEDAL_REF -DDAAL_CPU=rv64 -Werror -Wreturn-type \
+                     -Wno-unused-command-line-argument \
                      $(COMPILER.lnx.clang.target) \
                      $(COMPILER.sysroot)
 
--
2.43.0
